This file is the attribution mechanism required by section 4(d) of the Apache
License and by the specification's open-source policy (docs/21 section 35). It
is the accumulation point for attribution notices that must travel with a
redistribution -- not a dependency inventory.

The dependency inventory is the SBOM. A CycloneDX 1.6 SBOM is generated per
image and per lockfile and attached to each release; see SECURITY.md. Do not
duplicate it here, because a hand-maintained copy drifts from the build and a
stale attribution list is worse than a generated one.

What belongs in this file:

  * A NOTICE file carried by an Apache-2.0 dependency. Section 4(d) requires
    those contents to be reproduced in redistributions; that is not satisfied by
    an SBOM row.

  * Attribution required by a permissive licence that asks for it by name --
    BSD-3-Clause, MIT where a project asks for the notice to travel, and similar.

  * MODEL WEIGHT LICENCES. These are the attributions most likely to be missed,
    because downloaded model artifacts appear in no SBOM, are invisible to every
    dependency scanner, and carry their own terms. Each entry names the model,
    its pinned revision, and its licence. The pins themselves live in
    services/ai-service/models.manifest.toml, which the licence gate reads.

  * Any component whose licence terms a self-hoster inherits by running our
    images, where the terms require the notice to be visible to them.

